{"record_id":"D42-B75-R004","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B75","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Secret Non-Exposure Test","objective":"Verify that sensitive secret values are not emitted through logs, errors, traces, test output, or ordinary API responses.","precondition":"Controlled synthetic secrets are available and observable output channels are identified.","input":"Operations involving synthetic secret values under normal and failure conditions.","action":"Execute the operations and inspect relevant output channels for secret material or unsafe representations.","expected_result":"Secret values remain within their permitted handling boundary.","pass_criteria":"No prohibited secret value appears in tested output channels.","failure_interpretation":"Secret exposure indicates logging, error-handling, tracing, serialization, or data-flow defects.","implementation_relevance":"Tests sensitive-data handling throughout the execution pipeline.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Use synthetic secrets and secure test-artifact handling; never place real production secrets into tests.","performance_considerations":"Secret-redaction mechanisms can add processing overhead; correctness remains the primary requirement.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General secret-handling security testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B75-R005","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B75","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Security Failure Fail-Closed Test","objective":"Verify that security-control failures result in denial or another explicitly safe state rather than implicit permission.","precondition":"A security control has a defined fail-closed or equivalent failure policy.","input":"Controlled failure of the authorization, policy, validation, or security dependency.","action":"Trigger the control failure and attempt the protected operation.","expected_result":"The protected operation is blocked or handled according to the documented safe-failure policy.","pass_criteria":"No protected action succeeds solely because the security control became unavailable or failed unexpectedly.","failure_interpretation":"Successful protected action during control failure indicates a security fail-open defect.","implementation_relevance":"Critical for resilient autonomous systems with mandatory governance controls.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Test only in isolated environments and ensure failure injection cannot affect production security controls.","performance_considerations":"Fail-closed behavior may temporarily reduce availability; the security contract takes precedence over unverified performance assumptions.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General fail-closed security testing methodology."}

{"record_id":"D42-B76-R001","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B76","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Input Size Limit Test","objective":"Verify that documented input-size limits are enforced consistently at the relevant processing boundary.","precondition":"An explicit maximum size or resource limit is defined.","input":"Inputs below, at, and above the supported size boundary.","action":"Submit each input and inspect acceptance, rejection, and resource behavior.","expected_result":"Inputs within the limit are processed according to the contract and oversized inputs are rejected or handled according to policy.","pass_criteria":"Boundary behavior is deterministic and no oversized input bypasses the limit through alternate representation.","failure_interpretation":"Unbounded acceptance or inconsistent limit enforcement indicates a resource-protection defect.","implementation_relevance":"Supports resilience against accidental or adversarial resource exhaustion.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Size limits can mitigate denial-of-service and parser/resource-exhaustion risks.","performance_considerations":"Boundary tests should be performed with controlled resource limits; actual capacity requires measurement.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General resource-limit testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B76-R002","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B76","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Concurrency Limit Test","objective":"Verify that configured concurrency limits prevent unsupported simultaneous work while preserving recovery after capacity becomes available.","precondition":"A component has an explicit concurrency limit.","input":"Operations below, at, and above the configured concurrency boundary.","action":"Execute controlled concurrent work and observe acceptance, queuing, rejection, and recovery.","expected_result":"Concurrency behavior follows the declared capacity policy.","pass_criteria":"The system does not exceed the supported concurrency boundary and recovers when active work completes.","failure_interpretation":"Unbounded concurrency, permanent starvation, or incorrect rejection indicates capacity-control defects.","implementation_relevance":"Tests protection against resource exhaustion in concurrent services and workers.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Concurrency controls can protect shared resources from abuse and accidental overload.","performance_considerations":"The configured limit is a policy value, not a universal performance benchmark; actual capacity requires measurement.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General concurrency-limit testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B76-R003","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B76","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Rate-Limit Boundary Test","objective":"Verify that requests are accepted, limited, and restored according to the declared rate-limit policy.","precondition":"A controlled rate-limit policy and isolated test client exist.","input":"Requests below, at, and above the configured rate boundary.","action":"Send controlled request sequences and observe acceptance, limiting behavior, and recovery after the policy window.","expected_result":"Rate limiting follows the configured policy and does not incorrectly permit or reject requests outside the defined conditions.","pass_criteria":"Boundary behavior and reset semantics match the documented contract.","failure_interpretation":"Unexpected unlimited access or premature blocking indicates rate-limit implementation or state-tracking defects.","implementation_relevance":"Supports resilience and abuse-control verification.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Rate limits may protect authentication, public APIs, and expensive operations from abuse.","performance_considerations":"Rate-limit accounting adds overhead and should be measured only if performance is an explicit requirement.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General rate-limiting testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B76-R004","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B76","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Queue Backpressure Test","objective":"Verify that a producer exceeding downstream processing capacity experiences the documented backpressure behavior.","precondition":"A producer-consumer pipeline has explicit queue capacity and backpressure semantics.","input":"A controlled workload that exceeds consumer processing capacity.","action":"Increase production rate and observe queue state, producer behavior, and eventual recovery.","expected_result":"Backpressure limits queue growth or otherwise handles overload according to policy.","pass_criteria":"The queue does not exceed its supported resource boundary and the producer receives the documented response.","failure_interpretation":"Unbounded queue growth, silent loss, or producer deadlock indicates a backpressure defect.","implementation_relevance":"Tests resilience of asynchronous pipelines under overload.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Unbounded buffering can become a denial-of-service risk.","performance_considerations":"Backpressure behavior directly affects throughput and latency and should be measured when capacity objectives exist.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General backpressure testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B76-R005","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B76","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Resource Quota Enforcement Test","objective":"Verify that per-user, per-tenant, or per-operation resource quotas are enforced according to policy.","precondition":"A resource quota model with controlled test identities or scopes exists.","input":"Resource usage below, at, and above the applicable quota.","action":"Perform resource-consuming operations and inspect quota enforcement and recovery behavior.","expected_result":"Usage within quota is permitted and usage exceeding quota is blocked, delayed, or otherwise handled according to policy.","pass_criteria":"Quota boundaries are enforced consistently across supported access paths.","failure_interpretation":"Quota bypass or inconsistent enforcement indicates an isolation or resource-governance defect.","implementation_relevance":"Supports multi-tenant reliability and controlled resource allocation.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Quota enforcement can protect tenants from cross-tenant resource starvation.","performance_considerations":"Quota accounting introduces overhead; actual capacity must be measured under representative workloads.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General quota-enforcement testing methodology."}

