{"record_id":"D42-B77-R005","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B77","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Failure Diagnostic Sufficiency Test","objective":"Verify that important failure paths emit enough structured evidence to distinguish likely failure categories without exposing prohibited sensitive data.","precondition":"Failure-diagnostic requirements and permitted evidence fields are defined.","input":"Representative dependency, validation, authorization, timeout, and internal failure conditions.","action":"Trigger each controlled failure and inspect diagnostic evidence.","expected_result":"Diagnostics contain the required structured context and classify the failure within the supported taxonomy.","pass_criteria":"Evidence is sufficient for defined diagnosis tasks and contains no prohibited secret or sensitive content.","failure_interpretation":"Insufficient or misleading diagnostics reduce autonomous debugging reliability.","implementation_relevance":"Directly supports retrieval, diagnosis, repair selection, and learning from failures.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Diagnostics must balance forensic usefulness with data minimization and secret protection.","performance_considerations":"Detailed diagnostics can increase I/O and storage; evidence requirements should be risk-based.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"RECOMMENDATION","provenance":"Derived from evidence-driven debugging and observability principles."}

{"record_id":"D42-B78-R001","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B78","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Differential Implementation Test","objective":"Verify that two independently implemented components produce equivalent results for the supported input domain when equivalence is required.","precondition":"Two implementations and an explicit equivalence relation are available.","input":"Representative normal, boundary, and adversarial-safe test inputs.","action":"Execute both implementations with identical controlled inputs and compare outputs.","expected_result":"Outputs satisfy the defined equivalence relation.","pass_criteria":"No unexplained difference occurs within the tested supported domain.","failure_interpretation":"A difference requires classification as implementation defect, intentional semantic difference, undefined behavior, or oracle limitation.","implementation_relevance":"Supports migration, refactoring, compiler validation, and autonomous code transformation verification.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Differences in validation or authorization behavior require explicit security classification.","performance_considerations":"Differential testing compares correctness; performance differences require separate measurement.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General differential-testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B78-R002","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B78","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Metamorphic Relation Test","objective":"Verify that a defined transformation of input produces the correspondingly transformed output required by the metamorphic relation.","precondition":"A valid metamorphic relation for the tested operation is defined.","input":"A base input and one or more transformed inputs satisfying the relation preconditions.","action":"Execute the operation on the base and transformed inputs and evaluate the expected relation between outputs.","expected_result":"The observed outputs satisfy the declared metamorphic relation.","pass_criteria":"All applicable relation checks pass.","failure_interpretation":"Relation failure indicates a possible implementation defect, invalid relation assumption, or unsupported input domain.","implementation_relevance":"Provides test oracles where exact expected outputs are difficult to enumerate.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Relations must not assume transformations that weaken security validation or authorization semantics.","performance_considerations":"Metamorphic testing multiplies executions; test cost should be managed without reducing required coverage.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General metamorphic-testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B78-R003","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B78","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Round-Trip Transformation Test","objective":"Verify that an encode-transform-decode or equivalent transformation round trip preserves the required semantic information.","precondition":"A reversible or semantically preserving transformation contract exists.","input":"Representative supported values including boundary and nested cases.","action":"Apply the forward transformation and inverse transformation, then compare against the defined equivalence relation.","expected_result":"The round-trip result is equivalent to the original value under the transformation contract.","pass_criteria":"All supported test cases preserve required semantics.","failure_interpretation":"Data loss, ordering changes, type changes, or corruption indicates a transformation defect.","implementation_relevance":"Supports serializers, compilers, refactoring tools, migrations, and data pipelines.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Security metadata and access-control attributes must not be lost during transformation.","performance_considerations":"Transformation cost can be measured separately where throughput requirements exist.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General round-trip testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B78-R004","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B78","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Invariant Preservation Test","objective":"Verify that a transformation, refactor, migration, or optimization preserves explicitly declared system invariants.","precondition":"The relevant invariants are formally or operationally defined.","input":"Representative states before and after the tested transformation.","action":"Execute the transformation and evaluate every applicable invariant.","expected_result":"All required invariants remain true after transformation.","pass_criteria":"No required invariant is violated.","failure_interpretation":"An invariant violation indicates that the transformation changed behavior beyond its permitted scope.","implementation_relevance":"Provides a general verification mechanism for autonomous code modification.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Security and authorization invariants should be explicitly represented when they are within scope.","performance_considerations":"Invariant checking may add verification cost but must not be omitted when it is a required correctness condition.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General invariant-based testing methodology."}
{"record_id":"D42-B78-R005","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B78","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Oracle Consistency Test","objective":"Verify that the test oracle itself produces stable and logically consistent classifications for the cases within its declared scope.","precondition":"An automated or human-defined oracle determines expected outcomes.","input":"Repeated, boundary, valid, invalid, and intentionally ambiguous cases within the oracle scope.","action":"Apply the oracle repeatedly and compare classifications against authoritative specifications or invariants where available.","expected_result":"Oracle classifications remain consistent and explainable within scope.","pass_criteria":"No unexplained contradictory oracle result is observed.","failure_interpretation":"An unstable or incorrect oracle can create false failures or false confidence and requires correction before relying on dependent tests.","implementation_relevance":"Protects the quality of autonomous test generation and verification systems.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Security-test oracles require explicit scope and should not be treated as complete security proof unless justified.","performance_considerations":"Oracle complexity can dominate test cost; optimize only after establishing correctness.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"INFERENCE","provenance":"Derived from test-oracle quality principles."}

{"record_id":"D42-B79-R001","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B79","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Regression Test Selection Test","objective":"Verify that the selected regression suite covers the components and behaviors affected by a defined code change.","precondition":"A change set, dependency graph, ownership map, or equivalent impact model is available.","input":"A representative code change with known direct and indirect impact.","action":"Generate or select regression tests from the impact model and compare coverage against known affected behavior.","expected_result":"All required affected behaviors have corresponding regression coverage.","pass_criteria":"No known impacted behavior is omitted without explicit justification.","failure_interpretation":"Missing impacted tests indicate an incomplete impact-analysis or regression-selection defect.","implementation_relevance":"Supports efficient autonomous test selection without relying on full-suite execution for every change.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Security-sensitive dependencies require explicit regression coverage when affected.","performance_considerations":"Selective regression reduces execution cost only if impact analysis is sufficiently reliable.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"RECOMMENDATION","provenance":"Derived from change-impact and regression-testing methodology."}
