{"record_id":"D42-B79-R003","dataset":"D42","dataset_title":"Test Cases","batch":"B79","knowledge_type":"TEST_CASE","title":"Backward Compatibility Regression Test","objective":"Verify that a change preserves explicitly supported existing behavior while introducing the intended new behavior.","precondition":"A compatibility contract and baseline behavior are documented.","input":"Existing supported use cases plus the new or changed use case.","action":"Run baseline-compatible tests and new behavior tests against the changed implementation.","expected_result":"Supported legacy behavior remains valid and the intended change is observable.","pass_criteria":"No unexplained supported behavior regression occurs.","failure_interpretation":"A regression indicates an unintended breaking change or an incorrectly specified compatibility boundary.","implementation_relevance":"Supports safe API, schema, library, and language evolution.","code_applicability":"HIGH","security_considerations":"Backward compatibility must not require preserving obsolete unsafe security behavior.","performance_considerations":"Compatibility layers can add overhead and should be measured only where required.","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":"General backward-compatibility regression methodology."}
