{"record_id":"D44-B01-R002","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B01","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Off-by-One Collection and Index Boundaries","problem_statement":"Index-based operations commonly fail at the first valid index, last valid index, empty collection, or first invalid index.","context":"Code accesses arrays, lists, strings, buffers, slices, ranges, or indexed records.","preconditions":["The collection has a defined indexing model.","Valid and invalid index semantics are known."],"inputs":["empty collection","single-element collection","first valid index","last valid index","first invalid index"],"expected_behavior":["Valid indexes resolve to the intended element.","Invalid indexes produce the contractually defined error or fallback.","Empty collections do not accidentally expose nonexistent elements."],"implementation_guidance":["Prefer iteration or range abstractions where direct indexing is unnecessary.","Make inclusive/exclusive range semantics explicit.","Avoid deriving an upper bound independently from the collection length when the API already supplies safe iteration semantics."],"failure_modes":["IndexError or equivalent boundary exception","skipped final element","duplicated first or last element","negative-index surprise behavior","empty-collection dereference"],"edge_cases":["negative indexes in languages that support them","slice endpoints equal to collection length","single-element collection","nested empty collections"],"security_considerations":["Incorrect bounds can cause memory-safety failures in unsafe languages or information disclosure in poorly isolated systems.","Bounds validation must occur before unsafe access."],"performance_considerations":["Repeated boundary checks inside hot loops may matter, but correctness must not be removed without validated optimization evidence."],"version_scope":"Indexing and slicing behavior is language/version dependent and must be resolved against the target language specification.","test_considerations":["Include empty, one-element, two-element, and normal collections.","Test first, last, and first-invalid indexes separately."],"verification_requirements":["Verify both semantic result and failure behavior.","For unsafe languages, require memory-safety analysis or appropriate tooling where applicable."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Target language specification and standard-library collection documentation","evidence_role":"index and slicing semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B01-R001","D44-B02-R001"],"tested_by":["D42"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B01-R003","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B01","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Zero-Cardinality Input","problem_statement":"Operations that normally process one or more elements may encounter zero items, causing empty-result, division, initialization, or control-flow failures.","context":"Batch processors, aggregators, reducers, pagination, joins, searches, and collection transformations receive no elements.","preconditions":["The operation can legally receive an empty input.","The contract defines whether empty input is valid."],"inputs":["empty list","empty iterator","zero matching records","zero-length batch"],"expected_behavior":["The implementation follows the documented empty-input semantics.","Aggregations return a defined identity or explicit error where required.","No nonexistent element is accessed."],"implementation_guidance":["Define empty-input behavior at the API contract level.","Avoid implicit assumptions that a collection contains at least one element.","Use explicit initialization for accumulators where an identity exists."],"failure_modes":["unhandled exception","division by zero","uninitialized accumulator","incorrect null result","infinite loop caused by empty-progress assumptions"],"edge_cases":["empty input with required metadata","empty filtered result after nonempty source","all records rejected by validation","zero-page pagination result"],"security_considerations":["Empty authorization scopes must not accidentally mean unrestricted access.","Empty allowlists and denylists require explicit semantics."],"performance_considerations":["Empty work should generally avoid unnecessary downstream initialization or expensive resource allocation."],"test_considerations":["Test truly empty input and input that becomes empty after filtering.","Test empty input at every boundary where cardinality assumptions exist."],"verification_requirements":["Verify that the empty case has an explicit contract rather than relying on accidental library behavior."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable API, language, and library contracts","evidence_role":"empty-input semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B01-R002","D44-B02-R002"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B01-R004","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B01","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Degenerate Mathematical Domains","problem_statement":"Algorithms may encounter mathematically valid but degenerate inputs such as zero denominators, zero-length vectors, coincident points, singular matrices, or empty sets.","context":"Numerical, geometric, statistical, optimization, graph, or scientific algorithms operate on inputs where a normal mathematical assumption collapses.","preconditions":["The algorithm has mathematical preconditions beyond basic type validation.","Degenerate states can arise from legitimate upstream data."],"inputs":["zero denominator","zero-length vector","identical points","singular matrix","empty set"],"expected_behavior":["The implementation detects mathematical precondition violations before applying undefined operations.","Defined degenerate results are returned where mathematically valid.","Undefined cases are represented explicitly rather than silently producing misleading values."],"implementation_guidance":["Document mathematical preconditions.","Separate undefined, degenerate-but-defined, and ordinary cases.","Use numerically stable formulations where floating-point behavior is relevant."],"failure_modes":["division by zero","NaN propagation","infinite result interpreted as finite","singular-system failure","false convergence"],"edge_cases":["very small denominator","near-singular matrix","all points identical","zero variance","zero norm"],"security_considerations":["Malformed or adversarial numerical inputs can trigger resource amplification or exceptional control flow.","Input limits should prevent pathological numerical workloads where appropriate."],"performance_considerations":["Special-case handling may prevent expensive general algorithms from operating on degenerate inputs.","Numerical safeguards should not be described as performance improvements without measurement."],"test_considerations":["Cover exactly degenerate inputs and near-degenerate inputs separately.","Include expected failure semantics where no mathematical result exists."],"verification_requirements":["Verify mathematical preconditions against authoritative algorithm documentation or literature.","Do not classify approximate numerical behavior as exact without evidence."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Authoritative mathematical definition or algorithm specification","evidence_role":"domain and degeneracy semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B01-R001","D44-B10-R003"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B01-R005","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B01","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Empty or Singleton Structural Graphs","problem_statement":"Graph and tree algorithms often assume multiple vertices or edges and can fail on empty graphs, singleton graphs, isolated vertices, or root-only trees.","context":"Traversal, connectivity, shortest-path, dependency, topology, and hierarchy algorithms process graph-like structures.","preconditions":["The graph representation permits zero or one vertex.","The algorithm has defined applicability conditions."],"inputs":["empty graph","single vertex","single isolated vertex","root-only tree","graph with vertices but no edges"],"expected_behavior":["Structural cardinality is handled explicitly.","Algorithms that require a source or target report the absence clearly.","Connectivity and traversal semantics match the graph model."],"implementation_guidance":["Distinguish empty graph, singleton graph, and disconnected graph.","Avoid assuming an edge exists merely because vertices exist.","Define source/target behavior when either is absent."],"failure_modes":["missing-root exception","incorrect connectivity result","infinite traversal","invalid edge dereference","incorrect path reconstruction"],"edge_cases":["self-loop","parallel edge","isolated vertex","zero-edge graph","singleton source equal to target"],"security_considerations":["Graph-derived authorization or dependency decisions must not interpret missing relationships as unrestricted relationships."],"performance_considerations":["Empty and singleton structures should not trigger full-scale traversal machinery unnecessarily."],"test_considerations":["Test zero, one, and two vertices separately.","Test disconnected and isolated structures."],"verification_requirements":["Verify graph model assumptions before applying algorithm-specific correctness claims."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable graph algorithm specification or authoritative algorithm literature","evidence_role":"structural preconditions"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B01-R003","D44-B04-R001"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B02-R001","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B02","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Missing Versus Explicit Null","problem_statement":"A missing field and an explicitly supplied null-like value may carry different semantics, but implementations frequently collapse them into one state.","context":"APIs, configuration, database records, patches, optional parameters, and serialization formats support optional values.","preconditions":["The data model permits omission and/or null.","The contract assigns potentially different meanings to absence and explicit null."],"inputs":["field omitted","field present with null","field present with empty value","field present with default value"],"expected_behavior":["The implementation preserves semantic distinctions required by the contract.","Patch/update operations do not unintentionally overwrite values when a field is merely absent.","Serialization preserves required distinction."],"implementation_guidance":["Represent presence independently from value where semantics require it.","Document merge and patch behavior explicitly.","Avoid using a single sentinel for multiple semantic states without a defined contract."],"failure_modes":["unintended overwrite","incorrect defaulting","authorization bypass through omitted fields","serialization round-trip information loss"],"edge_cases":["nested missing field","null nested object","null collection versus empty collection","missing configuration key versus explicit null"],"security_considerations":["Missing security policy fields must not silently become permissive defaults.","Authorization decisions should distinguish unavailable policy data from an explicit deny/allow state."],"performance_considerations":["Presence tracking adds representation complexity but should not be removed merely for convenience where semantics require it."],"test_considerations":["Test omission, explicit null, empty value, and explicit default independently.","Test request parsing and persistence round trips."],"verification_requirements":["Verify field-presence semantics against the schema or API specification."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable API/schema/serialization specification","evidence_role":"presence and null semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B02-R002","D44-B08-R002"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B02-R002","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B02","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Empty String Versus Absent String","problem_statement":"Empty strings may be valid values, invalid values, or semantic equivalents of absence depending on the contract.","context":"User input, configuration, identifiers, headers, environment variables, database fields, and text APIs process string values.","preconditions":["The interface accepts strings.","The specification does not universally equate empty string with missing data."],"inputs":["missing string","empty string","single whitespace","trimmed empty string","nonempty string"],"expected_behavior":["The implementation applies the contractually defined distinction.","Normalization is performed only where explicitly required.","Identifiers are not silently changed by generic trimming or case conversion."],"implementation_guidance":["Validate presence and content separately when needed.","Define normalization before validation where normalization is part of the contract.","Do not treat whitespace as empty without an explicit normalization rule."],"failure_modes":["incorrect required-field acceptance","identifier collision","unexpected default selection","loss of intentional empty value"],"edge_cases":["string containing only Unicode whitespace","zero-width characters","newline-only value","empty password field","empty optional label"],"security_considerations":["Normalization inconsistencies can create validation bypasses.","Credential and identifier processing should use explicit canonicalization rules."],"performance_considerations":["Repeated normalization of large text values can be expensive; perform it at a well-defined boundary where possible."],"test_considerations":["Use ASCII and Unicode whitespace cases separately.","Test pre-normalized and post-normalized behavior."],"verification_requirements":["Verify normalization and emptiness semantics against the relevant protocol or application contract."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable API contract and Unicode normalization/character documentation","evidence_role":"text semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B02-R001","D44-B08-R003"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B02-R003","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Optional Configuration With Partial Presence","batch":"B02","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Partially Specified Configuration","problem_statement":"Configuration objects may contain only a subset of supported fields, requiring deterministic handling of defaults, inheritance, and validation.","context":"Applications load layered configuration from files, environment variables, command-line arguments, remote settings, or defaults.","preconditions":["Multiple configuration sources or optional settings exist.","Some fields have defaults or inherited values."],"inputs":["empty configuration","one override","partial nested configuration","conflicting source values"],"expected_behavior":["Defaults are applied deterministically.","Higher-precedence values override lower-precedence values only according to documented rules.","Missing required configuration is reported explicitly."],"implementation_guidance":["Define precedence as data, not implicit control flow.","Validate the resolved configuration after merging where appropriate.","Preserve provenance of configuration values when operational debugging requires it."],"failure_modes":["partial initialization","silent fallback to unsafe defaults","order-dependent configuration","nested merge corruption"],"edge_cases":["empty nested object","null nested object","unknown configuration key","default overridden by empty value"],"security_considerations":["Security-sensitive configuration should fail closed when required policy values are unavailable.","Unknown configuration keys should not silently alter security behavior."],"performance_considerations":["Configuration resolution normally occurs infrequently; optimize only when profiling demonstrates a real cost."],"test_considerations":["Test each source independently and combinations of precedence.","Test missing required fields after resolution."],"verification_requirements":["Verify resolved configuration against schema and precedence rules."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Application configuration specification and applicable framework documentation","evidence_role":"configuration semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B02-R001","D44-B07-R002"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B02-R004","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B02","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Duplicate Logical Input","problem_statement":"An input collection can contain multiple representations of the same logical entity, causing duplicate processing or inconsistent aggregation.","context":"Imports, API requests, event streams, batch files, and synchronization systems process collections of logically identifiable records.","preconditions":["A stable logical identity or deduplication criterion exists.","Duplicates can arrive legitimately or through upstream retries."],"inputs":["unique records","exact duplicates","same identity with differing payload","duplicates separated by unrelated records"],"expected_behavior":["The implementation follows the specified duplicate policy.","Identical duplicates do not cause unintended repeated side effects where idempotency is required.","Conflicting duplicates are not silently merged without a defined rule."],"implementation_guidance":["Define identity separately from payload equality.","Use idempotency keys or deterministic identity where appropriate.","Treat conflicting duplicates as a distinct condition from exact duplicates."],"failure_modes":["double charge","duplicate record creation","last-write-wins corruption","inconsistent aggregate totals"],"edge_cases":["duplicate within one request","duplicate across retries","same identity with stale version","same identity with conflicting immutable fields"],"security_considerations":["Duplicate identity handling can become an authorization bypass if ownership checks are applied inconsistently.","Replay protection may be required for security-sensitive actions."],"performance_considerations":["Deduplication structures consume memory proportional to retained identity state; choose bounded strategies where streams are large."],"test_considerations":["Test exact duplicate and conflicting duplicate separately.","Test duplicates across retries and batch