{"record_id":"D44-B02-R005","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B02","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Conflicting Representations of the Same Entity","problem_statement":"Two records may refer to the same logical entity while disagreeing on mutable or immutable fields.","context":"Synchronization, replication, import/export, merge, caching, and distributed update systems reconcile records from multiple sources.","preconditions":["Logical identity can be established.","Records may originate from different authorities or versions."],"inputs":["identical records","same identity with newer version","same identity with stale version","same identity with conflicting immutable data"],"expected_behavior":["Conflict policy is explicit and deterministic.","Authoritative or versioned data is selected according to defined rules.","Unresolvable conflicts are surfaced rather than silently discarded."],"implementation_guidance":["Separate identity resolution from conflict resolution.","Use version, timestamp, authority, or domain-specific conflict rules only when justified by the system contract.","Retain conflict evidence when auditability matters."],"failure_modes":["lost update","silent data corruption","oscillating synchronization","incorrect source-of-truth selection"],"edge_cases":["equal timestamps","clock skew","missing version","same version with different payload","conflict during retry"],"security_considerations":["An untrusted source must not override authoritative security metadata merely because it is newer.","Conflict resolution must respect trust boundaries and authorization."],"performance_considerations":["Conflict detection may require retaining version metadata or additional comparisons; do not assume negligible cost at scale."],"test_considerations":["Test equal, older, newer, and conflicting versions.","Test behavior when conflict metadata is missing."],"verification_requirements":["Verify conflict policy against domain requirements and