{"record_id":"D44-B03-R001","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B03","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Type Boundary and Representation Mismatch","problem_statement":"A value can be semantically valid while its concrete representation differs across layers, such as integer versus string, signed versus unsigned, or date versus timestamp.","context":"Data crosses API, serialization, storage, language, or database boundaries.","preconditions":["Multiple representations of the same logical value exist.","Conversion rules are not inherently identical across systems."],"inputs":["numeric string","numeric value","signed value","unsigned representation","serialized timestamp"],"expected_behavior":["Conversions preserve the intended semantic value.","Unsupported or lossy conversions are rejected or explicitly documented.","No implicit coercion changes the meaning silently."],"implementation_guidance":["Define canonical representations at boundaries.","Perform explicit conversion and validation.","Record precision and range constraints where representations differ."],"failure_modes":["overflow during conversion","precision loss","sign interpretation error","timezone shift","string-to-number coercion surprises"],"edge_cases":["maximum representable source value","negative value sent to unsigned target","floating value converted to integer","large integer serialized through a limited representation"],"security_considerations":["Type confusion can bypass validation and access controls.","Canonicalize before security-sensitive comparisons where the protocol requires it."],"performance_considerations":["Conversion overhead is usually secondary to correctness; optimize only after measurement."],"test_considerations":["Test exact boundaries and lossy conversions.","Test each serialization/deserialization boundary independently."],"verification_requirements":["Verify conversion semantics against source and target type specifications."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable language, serialization, and protocol specifications","evidence_role":"type and representation semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B01-R001","D44-B08-R001"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B03-R002","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B03","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Heterogeneous Collection Elements","problem_statement":"Collections may contain elements with different concrete types or shapes even when the nominal interface permits them.","context":"Dynamic languages, deserialized payloads, plugin systems, polymorphic APIs, and loosely typed data stores process mixed values.","preconditions":["The collection contract permits multiple types or runtime values.","Downstream operations may assume homogeneity."],"inputs":["all expected type","mixed supported types","unexpected runtime type","nested heterogeneous structure"],"expected_behavior":["Supported variants are dispatched according to explicit rules.","Unsupported variants are rejected with actionable diagnostics.","Type assumptions do not rely solely on nominal container metadata."],"implementation_guidance":["Use explicit discriminators or runtime validation where polymorphism is intentional.","Keep variant-specific behavior isolated.","Avoid broad coercion merely to force heterogeneous values into one path."],"failure_modes":["attribute/type error","incorrect branch selection","partial processing","unsafe cast"],"edge_cases":["subclass with overridden behavior","missing discriminator","unknown future variant","nested variant mismatch"],"security_considerations":["Untrusted polymorphic input requires strict type and discriminator validation.","Unsafe deserialization must not instantiate arbitrary types."],"performance_considerations":["Runtime validation can add cost to large collections; place validation at a boundary rather than duplicating it unnecessarily."],"test_considerations":["Cover every supported variant and at least one unsupported variant.","Test mixed collections rather than only homogeneous collections."],"verification_requirements":["Verify accepted runtime types against the actual contract.","Do not infer safety from static typing alone when data is externally supplied."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable language type system and serialization documentation","evidence_role":"runtime type semantics"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B03-R001","D44-B09-R003"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B03-R003","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B03","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Shape and Cardinality Mismatch","problem_statement":"Structured data can have the correct general type but an unexpected dimensionality, field count, nesting depth, or cardinality.","context":"Matrices, tensors, tabular records, JSON objects, tuples, function arguments, and database result sets rely on structural shape.","preconditions":["The operation expects a specific shape or cardinality.","Input shape can vary at runtime."],"inputs":["expected shape","zero-dimensional structure","one-element structure","extra fields/elements","missing fields/elements"],"expected_behavior":["Accepted shapes are validated before operations requiring them.","Unexpected shapes produce deterministic errors or defined coercions.","No implicit truncation or padding occurs unless specified."],"implementation_guidance":["Validate shape at the boundary where it becomes semantically required.","Distinguish missing, extra, and reordered elements.","Avoid relying on downstream exceptions as the primary validation mechanism."],"failure_modes":["dimension mismatch","wrong field mapping","silent truncation","incorrect broadcasting","positional argument shift"],"edge_cases":["empty dimension","singleton dimension","deeply nested empty structure","extra unknown field","duplicate field name"],"security_considerations":["Unexpected shape can be used for parser/resource amplification or validation bypasses.","Limit nesting and structural size where inputs are untrusted."],"performance_considerations":["Deep structural validation can be expensive for large payloads; enforce bounded depth and size."],"test_considerations":["Test zero, singleton, expected, missing, and extra dimensions/fields.","Test malformed nested structures."],"verification_requirements":["Verify structural requirements against the API or algorithm contract."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable schema, API, and algorithm specification","evidence_role":"shape and cardinality requirements"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B03-R001","D44-B09-R002"],"requires_implementation":true}}

{"record_id":"D44-B03-R004","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B03","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Precision Loss at Representation Boundaries","problem_statement":"A value may remain syntactically valid while losing information when converted between representations with different precision.","context":"Floating-point, decimal, timestamp, identifier, serialization, and numeric database boundaries may have different precision guarantees.","preconditions":["Source and target representations have different precision or range.","The application requires preservation of some or all original information."],"inputs":["exactly representable value","value requiring rounding","very small magnitude","very large magnitude","high-precision decimal"],"expected_behavior":["Lossy conversion is detected or explicitly accepted according to the contract.","Precision-sensitive values are not compared using inappropriate exact equality.","Persisted values retain the required precision."],"implementation_guidance":["Choose representations based on domain precision requirements.","Make rounding mode explicit where relevant.","Avoid binary floating-point for domains requiring exact decimal semantics unless the representation is specifically designed for it."],"failure_modes":["incorrect monetary value","timestamp collision","failed equality check","cumulative rounding drift"],"edge_cases":["halfway rounding values","subnormal floating-point values","very large exponent","repeated conversion cycles"],"security_considerations":["Precision loss can affect quotas, authorization thresholds, signatures, or financial controls.","Canonical representation should be established before security-sensitive comparison."],"performance_considerations":["Higher-precision arithmetic can have different computational costs; claims about trade-offs require measurement for the target workload."],"test_considerations":["Test values at precision boundaries and repeated round trips.","Te