{"record_id":"D44-B03-R005","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B03","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Unknown Future Variant","problem_statement":"A producer may introduce a valid new enum, discriminator, protocol value, or schema variant that an older consumer does not recognize.","context":"Versioned APIs, event schemas, configuration formats, plugin protocols, and distributed deployments evolve independently.","preconditions":["Producer and consumer versions may differ.","The protocol permits extension or version evolution."],"inputs":["known variant","unknown variant","deprecated variant","malformed variant"],"expected_behavior":["Unknown valid extensions are handled according to compatibility rules.","Consumers fail safely when they cannot process required semantics.","Unknown values are not silently mapped to an unrelated known value."],"implementation_guidance":["Define forward-compatibility behavior explicitly.","Preserve unknown data where round-trip compatibility requires it.","Separate unknown-but-valid from malformed input."],"failure_modes":["consumer crash","silent misinterpretation","data loss during round trip","incorrect default behavior"],"edge_cases":["unknown enum value","new optional field","new required field","new nested variant","future protocol extension"],"security_considerations":["Unknown security-related values should not default to permissive behavior.","Strict handling may be required when unknown semantics affect authorization or policy."],"performance_considerations":["Compatibility handling generally adds small parsing/branching overhead; avoid unsupported performance assumptions."],"test_considerations":["Test old consumer with future-compatible input.","Test unknown required semantics separately from unknown optional data."],"verification_requirements":["Verify compatibility behavior against the versioned protocol/schema contract."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verificat