{"record_id":"D44-B04-R001","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B04","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Initial-State Assumption Failure","problem_statement":"Code may assume an object, service, cache, database, workflow, or state machine has already been initialized when it is actually in its initial state.","context":"Lifecycle-driven software executes operations before initialization, after partial startup, or after state reset.","preconditions":["The component has distinguishable lifecycle states.","Operations may arrive before full initialization."],"inputs":["uninitialized state","partially initialized state","fully initialized state","reset state"],"expected_behavior":["Operations unavailable in the initial state are rejected or queued according to the contract.","Initialization is idempotent where required.","Partial initialization does not expose inconsistent state."],"implementation_guidance":["Model lifecycle states explicitly.","Avoid using incidental null checks as the complete lifecycle model.","Define which operations are valid in each state."],"failure_modes":["null dereference","partially configured operation","resource leak","inconsistent state exposure"],"edge_cases":["startup interrupted midway","initialization called twice","shutdown before initialization completes","restart from persisted partial state"],"security_considerations":["Security controls must not become active only after a late initialization step while requests are already accepted.","Fail closed when required security initialization has not completed."],"performance_considerations":["Repeated initialization checks should not dominate hot paths; lifecycle state should be managed at an appropriate boundary."],"test_considerations":["Test every lifecycle transition and invalid operation before initialization.","Test restart and partial initialization paths."],"verification_requirements":["Verify allowed operations for every documented lifecycle state."],"code_app