{"record_id":"D44-B04-R003","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B04","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Illegal State Transition With Valid Individual Operations","problem_statement":"Each operation may be valid in isolation but invalid when invoked from the current state.","context":"State machines, workflows, protocols, transactional systems, and authorization lifecycles enforce ordering constraints.","preconditions":["The system has explicit or implicit state transition rules.","Operation validity depends on current state."],"inputs":["valid operation in valid state","same operation in invalid state","repeated transition","skipped prerequisite transition"],"expected_behavior":["Only permitted transitions occur.","Illegal transitions produce deterministic failure or a documented no-op.","State remains unchanged when a transition is rejected."],"implementation_guidance":["Centralize transition rules or encode them in a state model.","Validate state before applying side effects.","Avoid changing state before all transition preconditions are satisfied."],"failure_modes":["state corruption","partial transition","side effect before rejection","invalid protocol sequence"],"edge_cases":["repeated transition","out-of-order message","transition after timeout","transition after external cancellation"],"security_considerations":["State-based authorization must be checked at the point of action, not assumed from an earlier state.","Do not let illegal transitions bypass approval or authorization stages."],"performance_considerations":["State validation should be cheap relative to the operation; correctness of transition ordering takes priority."],"test_considerations":["Test every legal transition and representative illegal transitions.","Verify state remains unchanged after rejected transitions."],"verification_requirements":["Verify transition invariants and side-effect ordering."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verifi