{"record_id":"D44-B11-R001","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B11","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Empty Dependency Graph","problem_statement":"Dependency resolution can encounter a project, module, or component with no dependencies, which must not be confused with an unresolved dependency state.","context":"Build systems, package managers, module loaders, plugin systems, and dependency injection frameworks resolve dependency graphs.","preconditions":["The dependency graph permits zero dependencies.","Resolution distinguishes an empty graph from a failed lookup."],"inputs":["zero dependencies","one dependency","missing dependency","cyclic dependency"],"expected_behavior":["An intentionally dependency-free component resolves successfully when allowed.","No artificial dependency is introduced merely because the graph is empty.","Missing dependencies remain distinguishable from zero dependencies."],"implementation_guidance":["Represent empty dependency sets explicitly.","Separate graph cardinality from resolution status.","Avoid assuming every component requires at least one dependency."],"failure_modes":["false unresolved error","unnecessary initialization","incorrect topological ordering","null graph handling failure"],"edge_cases":["root-only graph","optional dependency absent","all optional dependencies disabled","empty transitive closure"],"security_considerations":["An empty dependency set must not bypass required security initialization or policy components.","Dependency allowlists should distinguish intentionally empty from unavailable."],"performance_considerations":["Dependency-free components should avoid unnecessary graph traversal or resolver work."],"test_considerations":["Test zero, one, and multiple dependencies.","Test empty graph versus failed dependency resolution separately."],"verification_requirements":["Verify graph state and resolver status independently."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTE