{"record_id":"D44-B11-R002","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B11","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Dependency Version Boundary","problem_statement":"A dependency may satisfy a version constraint at one boundary while becoming incompatible immediately outside that boundary.","context":"Package managers, build systems, plugins, libraries, and runtime integrations use version constraints.","preconditions":["Dependencies have explicit or implicit compatibility ranges.","Version comparison semantics are defined."],"inputs":["minimum supported version","maximum supported version","just below minimum","just above maximum","pre-release version"],"expected_behavior":["Supported versions are accepted according to the declared constraint.","Unsupported versions are rejected or isolated before incompatible execution.","Pre-release handling follows the versioning contract."],"implementation_guidance":["Use the ecosystem's authoritative version-comparison semantics.","Avoid lexical version comparison when semantic version ordering is required.","Keep compatibility constraints explicit and reviewable."],"failure_modes":["incorrect dependency selection","runtime API mismatch","silent downgrade","unexpected pre-release selection"],"edge_cases":["0.x versions","build metadata","pre-release identifiers","open-ended upper range","transitive conflicting constraints"],"security_considerations":["Dependency resolution must not silently select an insecure or unapproved version merely to satisfy another constraint.","Integrity and provenance of resolved dependencies should be verified."],"performance_considerations":["Complex resolution can increase build or startup time; optimize resolver behavior only with measured evidence."],"test_considerations":["Test exact boundaries and adjacent versions.","Test transitive conflicts and pre-release versions separately."],"verification_requirements":["Verify version ordering and compatibility against the target ecosystem spe