{"record_id":"D44-B11-R003","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B11","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Optional Dependency Becomes Required Indirectly","problem_statement":"An optional dependency can become operationally required when a selected feature, plugin, code path, or configuration activates functionality that assumes its presence.","context":"Feature flags, plugin architectures, optional packages, and modular applications support conditional dependencies.","preconditions":["Dependencies can be optional under some configurations.","Features can change dependency requirements."],"inputs":["feature disabled","feature enabled with dependency present","feature enabled with dependency absent","dependency unavailable at runtime"],"expected_behavior":["Dependency requirements are derived from the active feature configuration.","Missing required runtime dependencies fail clearly before unsafe partial execution.","Disabled features do not require unnecessary dependencies unless specified."],"implementation_guidance":["Model conditional dependencies explicitly.","Validate feature-dependent dependencies during configuration resolution.","Avoid hiding dependency requirements inside late runtime failures."],"failure_modes":["startup succeeds then feature crashes","partial feature activation","silent fallback to incorrect implementation"],"edge_cases":["feature enabled dynamically","dependency removed after startup","multiple features share optional dependency","fallback implementation unavailable"],"security_considerations":["Security features must never silently deactivate because an optional dependency is missing.","Security-critical dependencies should be classified as required for the affected configuration."],"performance_considerations":["Conditional loading can reduce startup/resource use, but claims require measurement."],"test_considerations":["Test every feature/dependency combination that changes required capability.","Test runtime remova