{"record_id":"D44-B11-R005","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B11","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Dependency Resolution Under Partial Availability","problem_statement":"A dependency graph can be syntactically resolvable while one required dependency is temporarily unavailable from the registry, network, local cache, or runtime environment.","context":"Package installation, build pipelines, plugin loading, and distributed service startup depend on external dependency sources.","preconditions":["Dependency artifacts are not all locally guaranteed to be available.","Resolution can occur during degraded connectivity or repository outage."],"inputs":["all dependencies available","one unavailable","cache hit","cache miss during outage"],"expected_behavior":["Unavailable dependencies are distinguished from nonexistent dependencies.","Offline/cache policy follows explicit requirements.","The system does not silently substitute an incompatible artifact."],"implementation_guidance":["Separate logical resolution from artifact acquisition.","Use verified local caches where offline operation is supported.","Fail clearly when a required artifact cannot be obtained."],"failure_modes":["partial installation","inconsistent environment","unverified substitution","non-reproducible build"],"edge_cases":["repository timeout","artifact deleted upstream","cache contains older version","network restored during retry"],"security_considerations":["Dependency fallback must preserve artifact integrity and trust policy.","Do not bypass signature, checksum, or source restrictions merely to restore availability."],"performance_considerations":["Repeated remote resolution can increase latency and load; bounded retries and caching should follow explicit policy."],"test_considerations":["Test repository unavailable, cache available, and cache unavailable cases.","Test integrity validation on cached artifacts."],"verification_requirements":["Verify artifact identity and int