{"record_id":"D44-B12-R001","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B12","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Filesystem Path Boundary","problem_statement":"Filesystem operations can encounter empty paths, root paths, relative paths, parent traversal, platform-specific separators, or paths resolving outside the intended scope.","context":"Applications create, read, write, move, delete, or enumerate filesystem resources.","preconditions":["The application accepts or constructs filesystem paths.","The target platform has defined path-resolution semantics."],"inputs":["empty path","relative path","absolute path","root path","parent traversal","symlink path"],"expected_behavior":["Paths resolve according to an explicit filesystem contract.","Operations outside the permitted root are rejected where confinement is required.","Platform-specific path behavior is handled intentionally."],"implementation_guidance":["Canonicalize and validate paths according to the platform and security requirement.","Do not use string prefix checks as a complete path-containment test.","Account for symbolic links and filesystem races where relevant."],"failure_modes":["path traversal","wrong file target","permission error","directory/file confusion"],"edge_cases":["root directory","trailing separator","case-insensitive filesystem","symbolic link","junction/reparse point"],"security_considerations":["Untrusted paths require containment validation and appropriate filesystem permissions.","TOCTOU protections may be required between path validation and use."],"performance_considerations":["Canonicalization and filesystem metadata calls add I/O; minimize redundant checks without weakening containment."],"test_considerations":["Test relative, absolute, traversal, symlink, and platform-specific paths.","Test containment after filesystem resolution, not only string normalization."],"verification_requirements":["Verify path semantics against the target operating system and language file