{"record_id":"D44-B12-R002","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B12","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Filesystem Resource Disappears Between Operations","problem_statement":"A file or directory can be removed, replaced, or renamed after discovery but before the subsequent operation uses it.","context":"Concurrent processes and external actors can modify filesystem state between metadata lookup and access.","preconditions":["Filesystem state is mutable by another actor.","The implementation performs multiple filesystem operations."],"inputs":["path exists then disappears","path replaced by another object","file renamed","permissions changed between operations"],"expected_behavior":["The implementation handles disappearance or replacement as an expected race condition.","Critical operations use atomic filesystem primitives where available.","Errors do not cause unsafe fallback behavior."],"implementation_guidance":["Prefer atomic open/create/rename primitives when supported.","Avoid relying on a prior existence check as proof of future availability.","Handle file-not-found and replacement races explicitly."],"failure_modes":["TOCTOU vulnerability","wrong file accessed","unexpected deletion failure","stale metadata use"],"edge_cases":["symlink replacement","directory replaced","file truncated concurrently","permission changed"],"security_considerations":["Filesystem races can convert a valid path check into access to an unintended resource.","Use descriptor-based or atomic operations where supported and required."],"performance_considerations":["Atomic filesystem operations can reduce redundant metadata calls as well as improve correctness, but exact behavior is platform dependent."],"test_considerations":["Force concurrent replacement/removal between discovery and use.","Test both benign and adversarial races."],"verification_requirements":["Verify the actual filesystem primitive semantics on the target platform."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED