{"record_id":"D44-B22-R001","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B22","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Concurrent Read During Update","problem_statement":"A reader observes shared state while another execution context is modifying it, producing a partially updated or inconsistent view.","context":"The issue can occur in in-memory state, shared caches, configuration, indexes, or other mutable structures.","preconditions":["Shared state is readable and mutable.","Reads and writes can overlap."],"inputs":["Concurrent reader","Concurrent writer"],"expected_behavior":["Expose a consistent state according to the concurrency contract.","Use synchronization, atomic replacement, immutable snapshots, or an appropriate concurrent data structure where required."],"implementation_guidance":["Identify the consistency requirement before selecting synchronization.","Prefer atomic state replacement for immutable snapshots when practical.","Avoid assuming that individual operations being thread-safe makes a multi-step sequence atomic."],"failure_modes":["Torn state.","Lost update.","Inconsistent derived values.","Race-dependent behavior."],"edge_cases":["Reader starts immediately before commit.","Reader starts during multi-field update.","Multiple readers during repeated updates."],"security_considerations":["Security policy state must not be observed partially or inconsistently."],"performance_considerations":["Strong synchronization can reduce concurrency; measure contention rather than assuming a synchronization strategy is free."],"test_considerations":["Use controlled concurrency tests.","Repeat schedules where feasible.","Verify invariants rather than relying only on absence of exceptions."],"verification_requirements":["Verify the required consistency model.","Verify every shared mutable state transition has an appropriate concurrency mechanism."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUT