{"record_id":"D44-B32-R003","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B32","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Rollback With External Side Effect","problem_statement":"A local transaction rolls back after an external side effect has already occurred, leaving local and external state inconsistent.","context":"External calls, messages, filesystem operations, and third-party APIs generally do not share the same transaction boundary.","preconditions":["A workflow combines transactional local state with external side effects.","The local transaction can fail after the external action."],"inputs":["External action succeeds","Local transaction subsequently fails"],"expected_behavior":["Use compensation, an outbox/workflow pattern, reconciliation, or another explicit consistency strategy.","Do not assume local rollback reverses external effects."],"implementation_guidance":["Identify every side effect outside the transaction boundary.","Persist intent before executing external effects when durable coordination is required.","Design recovery for partial completion."],"failure_modes":["Orphaned external resource.","Local state says operation failed while external system succeeded.","Repeated compensation creates additional side effects."],"edge_cases":["External timeout with unknown completion.","External success followed by local crash.","Compensation itself fails."],"security_considerations":["Compensation and reconciliation must preserve authorization boundaries and must not execute broader privileges than the original operation."],"performance_considerations":["Durable coordination can add latency and storage overhead; choose according to consistency requirements."],"test_considerations":["Inject failure before and after external side effect.","Test compensation failure.","Test reconciliation of unknown external state."],"verification_requirements":["Verify every external side effect has an explicit failure/recovery strategy.","Verify local transaction boundaries do not falsely imply external atomicity."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Distributed transaction and external-side-effect consistency principles","evidence_role":"behavioral_basis","provenance_status":"SOURCE_NOT_VERIFIED"}],"relationships":{"related_to":["D44-B32-R002","D44-B32-R004"],"requires_implementation":true}}
{"record_id":"D44-B32-R004","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B32","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Nested Transaction Semantics Mismatch","problem_statement":"A nested operation assumes independent commit or rollback semantics that the underlying transaction mechanism does not provide.","context":"Libraries and databases differ in how nested transaction scopes, savepoints, and propagation semantics work.","preconditions":["An operation invokes another transactional operation.","The nested scope has its own apparent transaction boundary."],"inputs":["Outer transaction","Nested operation","Nested failure or commit"],"expected_behavior":["Apply the actual transaction propagation semantics.","Use savepoints or explicit compensation when independent rollback is required and supported."],"implementation_guidance":["Document transaction ownership.","Do not assume nested begin/commit calls create independent durable transactions.","Test propagation behavior explicitly."],"failure_modes":["Unexpected outer rollback.","Inner failure aborts unrelated work.","Inner commit is not durable until outer commit."],"edge_cases":["Nested savepoint rollback.","Exception caught by outer scope.","Multiple nested levels."],"security_considerations":["Authorization or audit state must not be considered durable before the authoritative transaction boundary commits."],"performance_considerations":["Nested savepoints or transaction coordination can add overhead."],"test_considerations":["Test nested success and failure.","Test outer rollback after nested success.","Test savepoint behavior where supported."],"verification_requirements":["Verify actual transaction propagation against the underlying platform.","Verify durable-state assumptions use the true commit boundary."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Applicable database/t