{"record_id":"D44-B32-R005","dataset":"D44","dataset_title":"Edge Cases","batch":"B32","knowledge_type":"EDGE_CASE","title":"Transaction Retry After Partial Failure","problem_statement":"A transaction or transaction-like operation is retried after an uncertain or partial failure, but the retry interacts with effects from the previous attempt.","context":"Retries can occur after deadlocks, serialization failures, transient connectivity errors, or ambiguous completion states.","preconditions":["The operation can be retried.","The first attempt may have partially completed or may have committed."],"inputs":["Initial transaction attempt","Transient failure or uncertain outcome","Retry"],"expected_behavior":["Retry only when the transaction model guarantees safe retry semantics or the operation has appropriate idempotency.","Re-establish a valid transaction context for the retry."],"implementation_guidance":["Treat retryable transaction errors according to the underlying system contract.","Avoid reusing invalid transaction state after failure.","Keep external side effects outside automatic retry unless they are explicitly safe."],"failure_modes":["Duplicate side effects.","Retrying a non-retryable transaction.","Using stale transaction state.","Data corruption from partial application."],"edge_cases":["Deadlock victim retry.","Serialization conflict.","Connection loss after commit.","External call inside retried transaction."],"security_considerations":["Repeated privileged operations must remain authorized and bounded across retries."],"performance_considerations":["Unbounded transaction retries can amplify contention and latency; use bounded attempts and backoff where appropriate."],"test_considerations":["Inject retryable and non-retryable failures.","Test unknown completion.","Verify external effects are not duplicated unexpectedly."],"verification_requirements":["Verify retry classification.","Verify each retry starts from a valid transaction state.","Verify side-ef