{"record_id":"D45-B14-R001","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B14","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_TEST_CASE","title":"Dependency Failure During Operation","problem_statement":"A required dependency fails while the primary operation is executing.","context":"The negative case verifies that dependency failure is contained and does not produce false success or corrupt partial state.","preconditions":["The operation depends on an external or internal component.","The dependency can fail during execution.","The operation has a defined failure policy."],"inputs":{"dependency":"forced failure","primary_operation":"valid operation"},"action":"Execute the operation while the dependency fails.","expected_result":["The operation reports failure or an explicitly documented degraded result.","No false success is reported.","Partial state is either rolled back, safely committed according to contract, or explicitly represented."],"pass_criteria":["The failure is observable at the correct boundary.","The final state conforms to the failure policy.","No false completion evidence is produced."],"failure_interpretation":"Returning success despite an unhandled required-dependency failure indicates incorrect failure propagation.","implementation_guidance":["Define dependency criticality explicitly.","Use transactional or compensating behavior where required.","Do not swallow exceptions merely to preserve apparent availability."],"failure_modes":["Exception is swallowed.","Fallback returns stale data without being marked degraded.","Partial writes survive without an explicit contract."],"security_considerations":["Failure handling must not bypass authorization or validation.","Fallback paths require the same security boundaries as primary paths."],"performance_considerations":["Timeouts and retries must be bounded.","Fallbacks should not create unbounded cascading work."],"test_considerations":["Inject dependency failure at multiple execution stages.","Test retry exha