{"record_id":"D45-B22-R003","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B22","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Missing Resource-Level Permission","problem_statement":"A principal has general access to a service but lacks permission for the specific resource or action requested.","context":"Resource-level authorization is required when access depends on ownership, scope, project, tenant, or resource attributes.","preconditions":["The caller is authenticated.","The service is generally accessible.","The target resource requires additional permission.","The caller lacks that permission."],"invalid_condition":["Resource-specific authorization condition is false."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Request targeting a protected resource."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The request is denied according to the resource policy.","The resource is not disclosed or modified."],"failure_interpretation":"Granting service-level access without resource-level authorization indicates incomplete policy enforcement.","implementation_guidance":["Evaluate resource ownership and policy attributes at the authoritative resource boundary.","Do not infer resource permission solely from service access."],"failure_modes":["Resource check omitted from one API path.","Cached object bypasses authorization.","Bulk endpoint applies weaker policy."],"security_considerations":["Resource-level authorization is a direct security boundary.","Test indirect access through search, export, cache, and asynchronous paths."],"performance_considerations":["Design authorization-aware data access patterns rather than retrieving unrestricted data and filtering afterward."],"test_considerations":["Test owned and unowned resources.","Test guessed identifiers and bulk access."],"verification_requirements":["Verify target ownership/scope and authorization decision.","Verify no unauthorized resource data or mutation occurred."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_sta