{"record_id":"D45-B22-R005","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B22","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Revoked Delegated Authority","problem_statement":"A delegated authority is used after the delegation has been revoked.","context":"Delegated operations must respect the current validity of the delegation rather than relying indefinitely on previously established authority.","preconditions":["A principal previously delegated authority to another principal or process.","The delegation has been revoked.","The delegate attempts the protected operation."],"invalid_condition":["Delegated authority is no longer valid."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Protected operation using revoked delegation."],"expected_failure_behavior":["Authorization is denied.","The revoked delegation cannot produce the protected effect."],"failure_interpretation":"Successful use of revoked delegated authority indicates stale authorization or revocation propagation failure.","implementation_guidance":["Define delegation lifetime and revocation semantics.","Bind delegated authority to an authoritative revocation mechanism."],"failure_modes":["Cached delegation remains active beyond policy.","Revocation is recorded but not propagated.","Different services use different delegation states."],"security_considerations":["Revocation guarantees should match the risk of the delegated action.","High-impact operations may require stronger freshness guarantees."],"performance_considerations":["Fresh revocation checks may increase latency; cache semantics must be explicit."],"test_considerations":["Test immediate revocation, delayed use, concurrent use, and expired delegation."],"verification_requirements":["Verify current delegation state and authorization result.","Verify no protected effect occurred after revocation."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_s