{"record_id":"D45-B26-R002","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B26","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Optimistic Concurrency Conflict","problem_statement":"An update is rejected because the version or concurrency token observed by the caller is no longer current.","context":"Optimistic concurrency prevents one writer from silently overwriting another writer's changes.","preconditions":["The resource uses a version or concurrency token.","Another update changes the authoritative version before the current update commits.","The current request uses a stale token."],"invalid_condition":["Submitted concurrency token does not match the authoritative version."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Update using stale version."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The update is rejected as a concurrency conflict.","The newer authoritative state remains intact."],"failure_interpretation":"Overwriting newer state despite a required concurrency check indicates lost-update protection failure.","implementation_guidance":["Perform the version check atomically with the update.","Return enough information for safe conflict resolution without exposing unauthorized data."],"failure_modes":["Check and update are separate operations.","Version token is omitted on one update path.","Conflict is silently retried with stale data."],"security_considerations":["Do not reveal protected resource state to unauthorized conflict responses."],"performance_considerations":["Conflict handling should avoid unbounded automatic retries."],"test_considerations":["Create controlled concurrent updates.","Test conflict resolution and repeated stale writes."],"verification_requirements":["Verify authoritative version after rejection.","Verify stale writer did not alter protected state."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Optimistic concurrency control and