{"record_id":"D45-B28-R003","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B28","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Network Destination Blocked by Policy","problem_statement":"An otherwise valid network request targets a destination explicitly prohibited by network policy.","context":"Network connectivity alone does not establish authorization to communicate with a destination.","preconditions":["Network access is technically available.","A destination policy exists.","The requested destination is prohibited."],"invalid_condition":["Destination violates network access policy."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Outbound network request."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The request is blocked before prohibited communication where policy requires pre-connect enforcement.","No successful external side effect occurs."],"failure_interpretation":"Allowing policy-prohibited network communication indicates egress-policy enforcement failure.","implementation_guidance":["Apply destination policy at the appropriate authoritative boundary.","Validate redirects and effective destinations where applicable."],"failure_modes":["Initial destination allowed but redirect becomes prohibited.","DNS resolution changes effective destination.","One network client bypasses centralized policy."],"security_considerations":["Network policy is a security boundary.","Do not rely only on caller-provided destination strings."],"performance_considerations":["Policy evaluation should be efficient enough for high-volume network operations."],"test_considerations":["Test blocked destinations, redirects, alternate representations, and concurrent requests."],"verification_requirements":["Verify effective destination and policy decision.","Verify no prohibited connection or external effect occurred."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Network egress-control a