{"record_id":"D45-B29-R001","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B29","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Unsupported Input Encoding","problem_statement":"Input cannot be decoded using the encoding required by the interface contract.","context":"Encoding failure must not be silently converted into replacement characters when exact data integrity is required.","preconditions":["An input encoding is declared or required.","The supplied bytes cannot be decoded according to that encoding."],"invalid_condition":["Decoding fails or produces invalid data under the contract."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Byte sequence using incompatible or malformed encoding."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The input is rejected or routed through an explicitly supported decoding policy.","No silently corrupted representation becomes authoritative state."],"failure_interpretation":"Replacing invalid data without contract support indicates data-integrity failure.","implementation_guidance":["Define encoding explicitly at boundaries.","Distinguish strict decoding from intentional replacement behavior."],"failure_modes":["Decoder silently replaces invalid bytes.","Different layers decode using different encodings.","Round-trip integrity is lost."],"security_considerations":["Encoding discrepancies can affect validation and security-sensitive comparisons.","Normalize only according to an explicit contract."],"performance_considerations":["Avoid repeated decode/re-encode cycles when a validated representation can be retained."],"test_considerations":["Test malformed byte sequences, unsupported encodings, and mixed encoding input."],"verification_requirements":["Verify decoded data preserves required integrity.","Verify rejected data does not enter trusted state."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_class":"VERIFIED_FACT","provenance":[{"reference_source":"Encoding-validation and data-integrit