{"record_id":"D45-B30-R001","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B30","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Negative Path Without Observable Evidence","problem_statement":"An operation fails but produces insufficient evidence to distinguish the failure from success, timeout, cancellation, or an unverified outcome.","context":"Autonomous engineering systems require trustworthy outcome classification; an error alone is insufficient when the durable effect is unknown.","preconditions":["An operation can fail or become uncertain.","Outcome classification is required by the consuming system.","Available evidence is incomplete or inconsistent."],"invalid_condition":["Failure path lacks sufficient evidence for reliable outcome classification."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Operation with incomplete outcome evidence."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The system records an explicitly uncertain or unverified outcome where confirmation is unavailable.","It does not fabricate success or confirmed failure."],"failure_interpretation":"Overstating an uncertain outcome is an evidence-integrity failure.","implementation_guidance":["Separate execution status from verification status.","Represent UNKNOWN or UNVERIFIED outcomes explicitly.","Preserve causal and provenance information."],"failure_modes":["Timeout becomes confirmed failure.","Exception becomes confirmed rollback.","Missing telemetry becomes assumed success."],"security_considerations":["Uncertain security-sensitive actions must not be treated as authorized or completed without evidence."],"performance_considerations":["Evidence collection should be proportionate to operation criticality."],"test_considerations":["Test lost responses, process crashes, network partitions, and incomplete telemetry.","Verify uncertainty classification."],"verification_requirements":["Verify that outcome claims do not exceed available evidence.","Require independent evidence for high-impact completion claims."],"code_applicabi