{"record_id":"D45-B30-R002","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B30","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Failure Without Rollback Verification","problem_statement":"An operation reports rollback after failure without independently verifying that the expected pre-operation state was actually restored.","context":"Rollback intent and rollback success are different claims and must not be conflated.","preconditions":["An operation can partially mutate state.","Rollback is attempted after failure.","Independent verification of final state is possible or required."],"invalid_condition":["Rollback completion is asserted without sufficient state evidence."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Failed operation followed by claimed rollback."],"expected_failure_behavior":["Rollback is classified as verified only when the required state evidence confirms restoration.","Otherwise the outcome remains unverified or partial."],"failure_interpretation":"Assuming rollback success from control flow alone creates false recovery evidence.","implementation_guidance":["Define explicit rollback invariants.","Verify durable state after recovery when the operation's impact warrants it."],"failure_modes":["Rollback function returns normally but leaves residual state.","External side effect cannot be reversed.","Verification reads stale state."],"security_considerations":["Security-sensitive rollback claims require strong evidence before restoring trust or access."],"performance_considerations":["Verification cost should be aligned with impact and consistency requirements."],"test_considerations":["Inject failures during rollback and verification.","Test partial recovery states."],"verification_requirements":["Verify the actual final state against the pre-operation invariant.","Do not label rollback VERIFIED solely because rollback code returned normally."],"code_applicability":"REQUIRED","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","verification_status":"SPECIFIED_NOT_EXECUTED","truth_clas