{"record_id":"D45-B30-R003","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B30","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Failure Hidden by Generic Success Response","problem_statement":"An internal failure is transformed into a generic success response that does not accurately represent whether the requested operation occurred.","context":"Error abstraction must preserve semantic outcome information even when implementation details are intentionally hidden from callers.","preconditions":["An internal operation can fail.","The external interface uses a simplified response model.","The failure affects whether the requested operation completed."],"invalid_condition":["External response asserts success despite insufficient completion evidence."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Internal failure mapped through external response."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The external contract accurately represents failure, pending, or unknown completion without exposing unnecessary internal details."],"failure_interpretation":"Generic success masking a material failure is an outcome-contract violation.","implementation_guidance":["Separate information hiding from outcome distortion.","Map internal errors to externally meaningful statuses deliberately."],"failure_modes":["All exceptions become HTTP/API success.","Monitoring sees success while durable state is incomplete.","Clients retry incorrectly because failure was hidden."],"security_considerations":["Do not leak internal diagnostics merely to provide transparency.","Security should not be used as justification for false success."],"performance_considerations":["Error mapping should not introduce expensive repeated diagnostics."],"test_considerations":["Test each material failure class and verify external outcome semantics.","Test client behavior after ambiguous outcomes."],"verification_requirements":["Verify external result accurately represents the strongest supported outcome claim.","Verify monitoring and audit records agre