{"record_id":"D45-B30-R004","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B30","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Failure Event Missing From Audit Trail","problem_statement":"A required negative outcome occurs but the system fails to record the evidence required for later diagnosis, governance, or verification.","context":"Negative cases are operationally incomplete when the system cannot later establish what failed, why it failed, and what state resulted.","preconditions":["The operation requires audit or outcome evidence.","The operation enters a defined failure state.","The failure event is not recorded or the record is incomplete."],"invalid_condition":["Required failure evidence is absent or materially incomplete."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Failure requiring audit evidence."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The failure is recorded with the minimum required provenance, outcome, timestamp, correlation identity, and relevant causal information.","If audit recording itself fails, the system enters its documented degraded evidence state."],"failure_interpretation":"Silent failure without required evidence reduces diagnosability and prevents reliable verification.","implementation_guidance":["Define mandatory audit fields by operation criticality.","Separate business success from audit-recording success when their consistency semantics differ.","Protect audit records from unauthorized modification."],"failure_modes":["Audit write occurs after state mutation and fails.","Failure record omits correlation identity.","Sensitive data is logged unnecessarily."],"security_considerations":["Audit records may contain sensitive information and require integrity and access controls.","Do not log secrets or unnecessary protected payloads."],"performance_considerations":["Audit overhead should be bounded while preserving required evidence.","High-volume negative events may require controlled aggregation without losing required evidence."],"test_considerations":["Tes