{"record_id":"D45-B30-R005","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B30","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Negative-Path Verification Produces Unsupported Claim","problem_statement":"A negative test or recovery procedure marks a failure as verified without executing or obtaining the evidence required for verification.","context":"A specified test is not equivalent to an executed test, and an executed failure is not automatically a verified system-state claim.","preconditions":["A negative case has defined verification requirements.","Required execution or evidence is absent.","A system or report attempts to mark the case verified."],"invalid_condition":["Verification status exceeds available execution and evidence."],"inputs_or_trigger":["Negative-case result with incomplete verification evidence."],"expected_failure_behavior":["The case remains explicitly unverified, specified-only, or unknown.","No unsupported VERIFIED status is assigned."],"failure_interpretation":"Claiming verification without corresponding evidence is a verification-integrity failure.","implementation_guidance":["Separate generated, parsed, executed, tested, passed, and verified states.","Persist execution evidence and verification evidence independently."],"failure_modes":["Test specification is counted as execution.","Process exit is counted as semantic success.","Generated output is treated as verified code."],"security_considerations":["Security-critical negative cases require evidence proportional to impact.","Never infer successful containment solely from intended control flow."],"performance_considerations":["Verification depth may be tiered by risk, but the selected tier must be explicit."],"test_considerations":["Track whether the negative case was actually executed.","Require evidence appropriate to the claimed verification level."],"verification_requirements":["Verify execution status, observed result, evidence source, and requirement satisfaction independen