{"record_id":"D45-B31-R002","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B31","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Duplicate Command Rejection","problem_statement":"A command that must execute only once is received again after the original request has already been accepted.","context":"The caller retries because the original response was lost or delayed.","preconditions":["The command has a stable idempotency key or equivalent identity.","The system records completed command identities."],"invalid_condition":["A previously accepted command identity is submitted again when duplicate execution is prohibited."],"inputs_or_trigger":["idempotency_key=cmd-123","same command submitted twice"],"expected_failure_behavior":["Do not execute the non-idempotent operation twice.","Return the documented duplicate or previously-completed result.","Preserve the original outcome and audit identity."],"failure_interpretation":["The duplicate request is not necessarily malformed.","The system must distinguish duplicate delivery from a genuinely new command."],"implementation_guidance":["Persist idempotency state atomically with the protected side effect where required.","Define retention semantics for idempotency records.","Do not generate a new identity during transport-level retry."],"failure_modes":["Duplicate side effect","Inconsistent retry result","Idempotency record race","Premature idempotency expiration"],"security_considerations":["Bind idempotency identity to the appropriate tenant, actor, authorization context, and operation scope when required.","Prevent unauthorized callers from probing another actor's command history."],"performance_considerations":["Idempotency storage should be bounded and indexed according to expected request volume and retention.","Avoid unbounded duplicate-history growth."],"test_considerations":["Submit identical commands sequentially and concurrently.","Test retry after a lost response.","Test duplicate requests from unauthorized