{"record_id":"D45-B31-R003","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B31","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Compare-And-Swap Predicate Failure","problem_statement":"A state transition must not occur because the supplied expected state no longer matches the authoritative state.","context":"The operation is conditional on an exact state predicate rather than merely on resource existence.","preconditions":["The operation includes an expected state or version predicate.","The authoritative state can change independently."],"invalid_condition":["The conditional predicate evaluates to false at the atomic decision point."],"inputs_or_trigger":["expected_status=READY","actual_status=RUNNING"],"expected_failure_behavior":["Reject the transition.","Leave the authoritative state unchanged by this failed operation.","Return a condition-conflict result that permits caller reconciliation."],"failure_interpretation":["The failed predicate is a normal negative control path, not evidence that the storage layer is unavailable."],"implementation_guidance":["Evaluate the predicate atomically with the state mutation.","Do not implement read-then-write checks that leave a race window.","Return sufficient structured information for safe reconciliation without leaking sensitive state."],"failure_modes":["TOCTOU race","Unauthorized state transition","Silent state corruption","False success"],"security_considerations":["State predicates must not replace authorization checks.","Do not expose protected state details merely to explain predicate failure."],"performance_considerations":["Atomic conditional operations can reduce round trips compared with separate read and write operations.","High contention can increase conflict frequency and retry load."],"test_considerations":["Race competing transitions against the same state.","Verify failed predicates produce no partial mutation.","Verify concurrent successful transitions cannot both claim the same exclusive state."],