{"record_id":"D45-B31-R005","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B31","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Conflicting State Transition","problem_statement":"A requested transition is invalid because the resource is currently in a state from which the transition is not permitted.","context":"State machines commonly reject operations whose source state does not satisfy transition rules.","preconditions":["A finite or explicitly defined state model exists.","The requested transition has a defined set of allowed source states."],"invalid_condition":["The current state is outside the transition's allowed source-state set."],"inputs_or_trigger":["current_state=CLOSED","requested_transition=START"],"expected_failure_behavior":["Reject the transition without applying partial state mutation.","Return a structured invalid-transition result.","Preserve the current authoritative state."],"failure_interpretation":["The request may be syntactically valid but semantically invalid for the current lifecycle state."],"implementation_guidance":["Encode transition rules explicitly rather than relying on scattered conditionals.","Validate the authoritative current state at the transition boundary.","Keep transition failure atomic."],"failure_modes":["Illegal state transition","Partial mutation","State machine corruption","Incorrect success response"],"security_considerations":["Authorization must be checked independently from transition validity.","Do not allow clients to select an arbitrary source state in the request."],"performance_considerations":["Explicit transition tables can provide predictable lookup cost and reduce repeated rule evaluation."],"test_considerations":["Test every forbidden source-target combination relevant to the state machine.","Test concurrent transitions from the same state.","Verify rejected transitions do not modify state."],"verification_requirements":["Verify transition rules are complete for supported states.","Verify forbidden