{"record_id":"D45-B32-R001","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B32","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Stale Read Used for Authorization","problem_statement":"An authorization-sensitive operation is attempted using state that was valid when read but is no longer authoritative.","context":"Authorization-relevant attributes can change between retrieval and action.","preconditions":["Authorization depends on mutable resource or actor state.","The operation uses previously retrieved state."],"invalid_condition":["The authorization decision is based on stale state at the action boundary."],"inputs_or_trigger":["permission_state_at_read=ALLOWED","permission_state_at_action=REVOKED"],"expected_failure_behavior":["Reject the action using authoritative authorization state.","Do not rely solely on the earlier cached or retrieved decision.","Record the authorization failure according to audit policy."],"failure_interpretation":["The failure represents stale authorization context rather than necessarily an authentication failure."],"implementation_guidance":["Minimize the gap between authorization evaluation and protected action.","Revalidate critical authorization conditions at the enforcement boundary.","Avoid treating client-supplied authorization state as authoritative."],"failure_modes":["Privilege use after revocation","TOCTOU authorization race","Stale policy enforcement"],"security_considerations":["Authorization must be enforced server-side at the protected resource boundary.","Sensitive actions require stronger freshness guarantees where necessary."],"performance_considerations":["Frequent authorization revalidation can add latency; cache policies must explicitly define acceptable staleness."],"test_considerations":["Revoke authorization between read and action.","Test concurrent role changes.","Test cached policy expiration during an operation."],"verification_requirements":["Verify revoked authorization cannot be used to complete protec