{"record_id":"D45-B33-R001","dataset":"D45","dataset_title":"Negative Cases","batch":"B33","knowledge_type":"NEGATIVE_CASE","title":"Unavailable Required Service","problem_statement":"An operation cannot proceed because a required downstream service is unavailable.","context":"The caller depends on a service that cannot currently accept or complete the required request.","preconditions":["The operation has a required downstream dependency.","The dependency is unavailable or unreachable."],"invalid_condition":["The required dependency cannot provide the required capability within the operation's permitted failure policy."],"inputs_or_trigger":["dependency_status=unavailable","operation_requires_dependency=true"],"expected_failure_behavior":["Fail without claiming the protected operation succeeded.","Return an explicit dependency failure or safe degraded result where defined.","Avoid partial side effects that imply completion."],"failure_interpretation":["The primary operation may be valid while execution is currently impossible because of dependency availability."],"implementation_guidance":["Classify dependencies as required or optional.","Define safe degradation separately from silent failure.","Propagate correlation information for diagnosis."],"failure_modes":["False success","Partial completion","Cascading failure","Unbounded retry"],"security_considerations":["Do not bypass authorization or validation merely because the normal dependency is unavailable.","Fallbacks must preserve equivalent security controls."],"performance_considerations":["Bound connection attempts and waiting time.","Prevent dependency failure from consuming all local worker capacity."],"test_considerations":["Simulate connection refusal, DNS failure, dependency overload, and dependency maintenance.","Verify required operations fail safely."],"verification_requirements":["Verify unavailable dependencies cannot produce a false successful outcome.","Verify fallback behavior matches documented s